      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T18:38:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the `let (offset, cmd_len) \u003d { ... };` block stay as it was, with only the `mm` lines added after it? Something like:\n\n```\n            (pin.offset as usize, pin.len as usize)\n        };\n\n        let current \u003d current!();\n        let mm \u003d current.mm().ok_or(EINVAL)?;\n        let page_mask \u003d mm.page_mask();\n```\n\nRe-indenting the upstream lines doesn\u0027t change behavior, and leaving them alone keeps conflicts with later ashmem changes from android17-6.18 down.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "bf0b454de922c159333f12bbabfc99b68bf29a84",
