        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T18:38:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried that with `mm.page_align()`, a `len \u003d\u003d 0` unpin from a 4KB process now stops at the 4KB-rounded size. For a 20KB region, the range ends 4KB into the last 16KB page, so `free_lru()` can only zero those 4KB instead of freeing the page as it did before this patch (`punch_hole()` only frees whole pages).\n\nWould `page_align(asma.size)` still work here? `mmap()` lets a 4KB process map up to the 16KB-rounded size, so 4KB processes could then pin and unpin any 4KB-aligned range they can map, as native processes can, and `Mm::page_align()` would have no user.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "bf0b454de922c159333f12bbabfc99b68bf29a84",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
